termination log and exit 3; others exit 1.\n- `internal/jobexec`: child in its own process group, stdout teed to `/out/stdout`, SIGTERM then SIGKILL after the grace period, exit 124 on deadline, orphan reaping on Linux (only when PID 1), group-read on `/work`, done marker written last with O_TRUNC and O_NOFOLLOW. A command that fails to start still writes the marker (127).\n- `internal/jobpost`: `GET /v1/result` only, key check, one-slot semaphore (429), 409 until the marker exists, then streams `tarball.Pack`. Shuts down on SIGTERM or the deadline and exits 0.\n- `docs/layout.md`: three lines.\n\n## Testing\nRan `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/jobexec`, and `go test` for gitx, cli, jobpre, jobexec, jobpost, docscheck, effects and cmd. All pass. A full `go test ./...` timed out at 2 minutes in this sandbox and was not completed.\nNew tests:\n- `TestCheckoutTree`.\n- `TestPre`: layout, read-only, history, missing SHA exits 3, symlink input exits 3, role repo mismatch, transient failure exits 1.\n- `TestPreBadSecrets` and `TestPreTokenNotInArgv`.\n- `TestExec*`: exit codes, tee, home, deadline, kill after grace, forwarded SIGTERM, grandchild, planted marker and modes, missing command, no argv.\n- `TestPost` and `TestRunKeyAndPort`.\n- `TestJobCommands`.\n\n## Open issues\n- The Authorization scheme for `job-post` is not defined in `jobpod`, so I used `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. #317's client must send the same.\n- Orphan reaping runs only when job-exec is PID 1 and only on Linux, so the unit tests cannot cover it. The kind-based test in #321 is the real check.\n- `job-exec` fails if `/job/home/.claude` already exists (a container restart). The pod should not restart this container.\n\nRequested next: `ard:review:eng-review`\nPR: [#399](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/pull/399)\nTests: passed\nOutput: [.ard/316/worker-engineer.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/222ee5b067c5dc530b297889d022f6895fb7dd0a/.ard/316/worker-engineer.md) · log [.ard/316/logs/worker-engineer-20261125T112946.474Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/222ee5b067c5dc530b297889d022f6895fb7dd0a/.ard/316/logs/worker-engineer-20261125T112946.474Z.log) · job `01M897G1JTF80XTC69XEAA46DA` · attempt 1\n\n\n# Plan for #316\n\n## Implementation\n\nAdopts the design-revision-3 plan in the comments (pre / exec / post), not the older fetch/exec/upload text in the issue body. Corrections against main: the shared workspace package is `internal/executor/workspace` (not `internal/workspace`); `jobpod.PreSecretDir`, `PostSecretDir`, `ItemManifest`, `ItemGitAccess`, `ItemResultKey`, `ResultPort`, `ResultPath`, `RootWork`, `RootOut`, `StdoutName`, `DoneName`, `ExitPermanent`, `ExitTransient`, `MountWork/Job/Out/Ctl/Bin`, `JobRole/JobSidecar/JobHistory/JobHome`, `AgentBin`, `Decode`, `KeyMatches` all exist already. Scrub and inputs come from the decoded manifest (`Manifest.Scrub`, `Manifest.Inputs`); the manifest has no TLS or fingerprint, and post serves plain HTTP.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. `internal/gitx/local.go` (new method, after `ExportTree`): `func (g *Git) CheckoutTree(ctx context.Context, gitDir, workTree, sha string) error` running `git --git-dir <gitDir> --work-tree <workTree> -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null checkout --detach --force <sha>` through the package's existing git runner. It keeps symlinks and exec bits and writes no `.git`. Reason: `ExportTree` refuses symlinks and caps at 64 MiB. Add the test (step 8) in the same step so the build stays green.\n2. `internal/cli/app.go`: add `JobPre`, `JobExec`, `JobPost` fields to `Handlers`, and the types `JobPreOpts{Deadline time.Time; GitBase string}`, `JobExecOpts{Deadline time.Time; Grace time.Duration; Argv []string}`, `JobPostOpts{Deadline time.Time}`. New `internal/cli/cmd_job.go` with three `Hidden: true` cobra commands `job-pre` (`--deadline`, `--git-base` default `https://github.com`), `job-exec` (`--deadline`, `--grace` default 10s, argv after `--` via `ArgsLenAtDash`; no argv returns `&ExitError{Code: 2}`), `job-post` (`--deadline`). `--deadline` is RFC 3339 UTC, parsed in cli; a bad value exits 2. Register in the root command like the other `cmd_*.go` files (follow `cmd_setup.go`). The nil-handler stub behaviour already applies.\n3. `internal/jobpre/pre.go` (new): `func Run(ctx context.Context, e *cli.Env, o cli.JobPreOpts) error`. Paths (secret dir, `/ctl`, `/work`, `/job`, `/ard-bin`, termination log) sit in an unexported package `paths` var so tests can redirect them; defaults come from `jobpod`.\n   - Read `manifest.json` and `token` from `jobpod.PreSecretDir`; `jobpod.Decode`. The token goes to git only as a `gitx.TokenFunc` (env via `pushEnv`), never argv. Set `HOME=/ctl/home`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` and umask 002.\n   - `InitBare(/ctl/repo.git)`; `FetchShallow(url, \"+<BaseSHA>:refs/ard/base\")`; when `Role.SHA != BaseSHA`, a second fetch of `R","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/ard-home/.claude/projects/-Users-al--ard-work-albertcbrown-ard-01M898CS7NH3JVHKB2KPK7ZW2F/eebbd6b7-4255-41b5-83d1-777caa2ad670/tool-results/bk6at2anh.txt","persistedOutputSize":35870},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PGBhAujrc1EcrW1AoSfZMt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
